# Version bump

GitFlare's version lives in `wrangler.jsonc` as `vars.GITFLARE_VERSION`. The same number is the `version` in `package.json` (and the root entries in `package-lock.json`), the fallback in both `GITFLARE_VERSION ?? '…'` spots in `src/index.ts`, and the account-menu footer in `src/dashboard/index.html` (`GitFlare v…`).

Every commit that changes product code bumps that number before the commit. Patch by default: `1.1.2` becomes `1.1.3`. Use a minor or major number only when the user names one.

Write the new number in all five places. Leave the CLI, MCP, client, and runner package versions alone unless those packages themselves changed.

```jsonc
// wrangler.jsonc
"GITFLARE_VERSION": "1.1.3"
```

```html
<!-- src/dashboard/index.html -->
<div class="menu-foot">GitFlare v1.1.3</div>
```
